### R3.2 (b) Page-Hinkley drift detector - EXECUTED

Faithful minimal port of river's 127-line detector (~40 lines stdlib; semantics confirmed against today's fetched source: dual CUSUM sums with -delta/+delta, running mean, reset after each alarm, test only once `n >= min_instances`):

```python
class PageHinkley:
    def __init__(self, min_instances=10, delta=0.005, threshold=8.0, alpha=1 - 0.0001):
        ...  # params; _reset(): _n=0, _x_mean=0.0, _sum_inc=0.0, _sum_dec=0.0,
             # _min_inc=+inf, _max_dec=-inf, drift_detected=False
    def update(self, x):
        if self.drift_detected: self._reset()
        self._n += 1
        self._x_mean += (x - self._x_mean) / self._n
        dev = x - self._x_mean
        self._sum_inc = self.alpha * self._sum_inc + dev - self.delta
        self._sum_dec = self.alpha * self._sum_dec + dev + self.delta
        self._min_inc = min(self._min_inc, self._sum_inc)
        self._max_dec = max(self._max_dec, self._sum_dec)
        self.drift_detected = (self._n >= self.min_instances and
            (self._sum_inc - self._min_inc > self.threshold or
             self._max_dec - self._sum_dec > self.threshold))
```

